.TH WLIST-DELETE 1 "17 November 2026" "version 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
wlist-delete \- remove item from registry.
.SH SYNOPSIS
wlist delete  [path/to/database]
[--item-id <item id>]
[--note-id <note id>]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove an item 
.B OR 
note from register.
.PP
By removing either, 
links established 
between the notes and items will be removed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --item-id <item id>
The id of the item to delete.
.TP
.B --note-id
The id of the note to delete.
.SH AUTHOR
Bryce Campbell (tonyhawk2100@gmail.com)
.SH EXAMPLES
Remove item from Registry:
.RS
.IP
wlist delete --item-id FF04C3DC-F0FE-472E-8737-0F4034C049F0
.RE
.PP
Remove note from Registry:
.RS
.IP
wlist --note-id 1
.RE